{%- comment -%}
  Strips the internal copywriting scaffolding out of a product description at
  render time.

  The descriptions are written to a house framework whose headings ended up
  live on the page as all-caps H2s: THE MOMENT, THE PROMISE, FEATURE TO
  BENEFIT, THE CLOSE. Those are notes to the writer, not to the customer.

  This removes them and leaves the prose to flow. Genuine content headings are
  emitted as written.

  It used to relabel them with `key | capitalize`, but `key` has already been
  through `downcase` for the drop comparison, and Liquid's capitalize lower-cases
  everything after the first character. A heading of more than one sentence came
  out as "24cm deep. gel memory foam. for the dog who has earned it.", and any
  brand or place name in a heading was lower-cased with it. It now prints `head`
  instead, so the copy renders exactly as written; `key` is still computed and
  still drives the drop match, so that behaviour is unchanged.

  The heading also stays an H2 rather than being demoted to H3. The product title
  is the page's H1 and the subheads inside a description are already H3s, so
  demoting the lead left the outline H1 -> H3 with nothing between, and the lead
  heading rendered at the same size as the subheads under it. `.pl-rte h2` is
  styled at 1.5rem against h3's 1.28rem in pl-styles.css, which is the size step
  this was always meant to have.

  Doing it here rather than by editing the descriptions means the product copy
  is never touched, every new product is handled automatically, and the whole
  thing is reversible in one commit.

  Usage: {% render 'pl-rte-clean', html: product.description %}
         {% render 'pl-rte-clean', html: product.description, drop: 'the moment,the close' %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign drops = drop | default: 'the moment,the promise,the close,feature to benefit' | downcase | split: ','
  assign chunks = html | split: '<h2>'
-%}
{{ chunks[0] }}
{%- for chunk in chunks offset: 1 -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign pair = chunk | split: '</h2>'
    assign head = pair[0]
    assign key = head | strip_html | downcase | strip
    assign body = chunk | remove_first: head | remove_first: '</h2>'
  -%}
  {%- unless drops contains key -%}<h2>{{ head | strip_html | strip }}</h2>{%- endunless -%}
  {{ body }}
{%- endfor -%}
